    "10:_": "the West to others, etc. And in Bishesh 20 Dam his wife does not eat with him, even though he brings her food, she needs to be mixed, since she does not eat from his dishes, and therefore he entitles her to a dezekiah for her soul. should involve themselves:",
    "11:_": "From the ground. A place where the city is placed on:",
    "13:_": "can't cook The second DIT is certainly a holy day, and therefore when he can do it on the second day, it is forbidden to do it on the first one, and it is forbidden to do it on the first one, and it is permissible to do it on the first day. Haul and there is a rape that cannot be baked on the Friday. It is permissible to bake on the the Master's Day for Shabbat by mixing the 23rd and 24th, for the beginning one must not bake except on the 10th so that a good dish for the Shabbat can be found (SAA):",
    "15:_": "We will eat the mixture. We were the stew (ASB), but if we eat the fet, there is nothing in it, and Efi' is 219 on the fifth day and on the Friday, and we remember the first 16th of the OT for the evening (ASKA2) (Yishash):",
    "16:_": "He can eat. And he will give him a second bread in Arabic, and he will be sent to him",
    "17:_": "He began to cook. It appears even if he did not yet leave the pot by the fire, only that he began preparing it such as cutting vegetables and the like — permitted to cook it, for there too in dough it deals that he began kneading and afterward permitted to bake:",
    "18:_": "Allow to sit. But they should not be allowed to take a seat of the sages:",
    "19:_": "It is allowed to turn on. This is what the Rebbe innovated from his mind. The Rabbi and the Rambam mentioned in the Irov and Adluki formula that it is permissible to light a Rega Shm Daf without an Irov, and in the same way, they believe that the Dach mention only the main part of the meal and all the other words of the meal. The S.C. and K.P. most of the judges and K.P. Yeshash, and the BH wrote that the Rabbi and the Rambam should rely on them to light a candle on Shabbat which is a mitzvah, and in Litha Hada Daha I wrote in the Rabbi and the Rambam is not frivolous about this and more.",
    "20:א": "(1) He will give his flour. In the draw and not in the KS Amash C. Shaz 7:",
    "20:ב": "(ב) If there is no name. It means that if there are others and don’t want to give them an assimi to a reduction and a “p",
    "20:ג": "(3) The melachot explicitly. Rashal wrote in responsum siman 78 it is forbidden to slaughter from Yom Tov to Shabbat since he did not specify explicitly in the eruv \"and to slaughter\"; Bach wrote and permitted for him, for all melachot before cooking are included, and cooking such as flaying and salting; and it appears he retracted since he did not write so in his composition — up to here; and in Rosh's responsum general 23:8 it implies explicitly permitted; Beit Yosef brought it; see what is written siman 503 and 538 seif 8 and 528; nevertheless it appears good to write explicitly \"and to slaughter\":",
    "20:ד": "(4) Do not cook for others. Since he cannot cook for himself and it is not permitted on behalf of him and he can ask about his vows without forgetting to cook on behalf of him, but here he is free to cook for himself without having to, such as to bake challah and the baker is not allowed to go to the ground, and he also says that he who fasts in the rabbi must study all day because his dainu fulfills half of it for you, he must fulfill all of it. Sessi 1912 is not sacred to begin with because and refer to Appendix PG Dapashim and this means that a servant is forbidden to cook for the sake of the clothing, the sign of the 1677 Amsh there and the 19th that applies to be the 1st, it is forbidden to cook the 19th for Shabbat and Afi' by mixing it is not enjoyable but on behalf of the non-complimentary of guests as in the 19th and 21st since it is forbidden to cook for others, it does not belong to the other 19th and 20th Bake and cook it:",
    "21:א": "(1) If he remembered, etc. Binyan Shlomo wrote: if he made a special dish for eruv tavshilin or designated it for that purpose, even if he intended to bless on it and forgot — permitted to cook, for blessings do not obstruct; and even if his wife designated without his knowledge — permitted — up to here; requires study why this is better than one who said and did not specify melachot explicitly forbidden as s.k. 20; and what he wrote blessings do not obstruct means if he said properly \"may it be,\" etc., and did not say the blessing — even though on erev Pesach permitted b'dieved without any statement, there the main action is joint participation; but here speech is primary to clarify a fine portion for Shabbat; therefore it appears one may not rely on this. Further he wrote nowadays if one forgot and did not make eruv — permitted, for the eruv text says \"for us and all Israel\" — if so each eruvs for all Israel; Bach wrote so; they did not examine people's actions well — we hold one must merit as s.k. 10; no person does this except one expert — therefore do not rely on this, siman 529:",
    "21:ב": "(2) 11 Dafi' 20. Esi' 133 Dafi' 29 Delma Shari:",
    "22:א": "(א) In the town, it is called. And you are blessed with your prayer",
    "22:ב": "(2) And some say Dai 33 20. Vishesh and 2H ruled as the first sabra 20 in the judgments of the Rabbi:",
    "23:_": "or accidentally. It's hard, Mai Kamlan Rama, because he wrote the OT by mistake and in the Bishesh, he wrote and M.M. by mistake. As such:",
